--- uploaded/_headers
+++ release/_headers
@@ -1,104 +1,9 @@
-# Security headers for static hosting providers that read a `_headers` file
-# (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages). This file is inert on providers that don't
-# read it (e.g. plain nginx/Apache/GitHub Pages) — apply the equivalent
-# headers at that layer's config instead (nginx `add_header`, Apache
-# `.htaccess` / vhost, CloudFront response-headers policy, etc.) using the
-# same directive values below.
-#
-# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-# RESOURCE AUDIT THIS CSP IS BASED ON (re-verify with tools/csp/*.js if the
-# app changes):
-#   - All scripts/styles/fonts/images load from same-origin local files only
-#     (assets/vendor/mathjax/**, assets/css/**, assets/js/**, practice/**).
-#     No external CDN, no third-party origin, anywhere in the render path.
-#   - fetch() calls (practice/data-loader.js) only ever request same-origin
-#     relative paths (../master-manifest.json, ../questions/**) — no
-#     cross-origin XHR/fetch exists.
-#   - Exactly 2 inline <script> blocks with no src= (the practice-id
-#     bootstrap and the MathJax config, both in practice/index.html) and
-#     0 inline <style> blocks. The landing page (index.html) and 404.html
-#     ship NO inline script and NO inline style: the catalog code lives in
-#     assets/js/theme.js, assets/js/catalog-model.js and
-#     assets/js/catalog.js, and its styles in assets/css/catalog.css.
-#     No inline style="" attributes and no element.style.cssText usage
-#     anywhere in the JS (only CSSOM custom-property writes, which CSP does
-#     not restrict). No eval()/new Function() anywhere.
-#   - fetch() on the landing page requests only same-origin relative
-#     files: master-manifest.json and assets/data/bank-index.json.
-#   - One <form> (the catalog search/filter form in index.html). It
-#     submits, if at all, to the same page with GET — form-action 'self'.
-#
-# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-# WHY style-src KEEPS PLAIN 'unsafe-inline' (no hash) — VERIFIED, NOT GUESSED:
-# An earlier version of this policy also hash-allowlisted style-src (for
-# a static inline <style> block index.html used to have) the same way script-src is
-# hashed below. That was tested against real Chromium across the full app
-# flow and BROKE MathJax: MathJax's CHTML output mode dynamically injects
-# and updates its own <style> element at runtime with computed font-metric
-# CSS (this is normal MathJax behavior, not a bug) — content that cannot be
-# known in advance and therefore cannot be pre-hashed. Per the CSP spec,
-# once style-src contains ANY hash-source, 'unsafe-inline' is ignored
-# entirely — so hashing style-src silently blocked MathJax's own styling
-# in every modern browser, confirmed by real "Refused to apply inline
-# style" console errors during `npm run test:browser`. MathJax is
-# explicitly off-limits to modify, so style-src stays 'self' 'unsafe-inline'
-# with NO hash-source — that is what keeps 'unsafe-inline' actually honored
-# for style-src, while script-src (see below) has no such runtime-injection
-# need and safely uses hashes. This trade-off is deliberate, verified, and
-# should not be "improved" without re-running `npm run test:browser`
-# against every math-containing bank first.
-#
-# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-# WHY script-src USES HASHES INSTEAD OF 'unsafe-inline':
-# script-src below allowlists this project's 2 specific inline <script>
-# blocks by SHA-256 hash (sha256-... below) rather than blanket
-# 'unsafe-inline'. Per the CSP spec, once ANY hash-source is present,
-# browsers that support hash-sources (all modern evergreen browsers)
-# ignore 'unsafe-inline' entirely for that directive and only execute
-# script that matches a listed hash — i.e. a page compromised via injected
-# inline script (XSS) can no longer just run arbitrary inline JS, closing
-# the exact gap 'unsafe-inline' leaves open. 'unsafe-inline' is still
-# listed afterward purely as a legacy fallback for pre-hash-source
-# browsers, which per spec ignore the hash-sources and fall back to it —
-# so this is real hardening in every current browser with zero regression
-# risk in old ones. Unlike style-src, MathJax and the rest of the app never
-# inject inline <script> at runtime (confirmed by the real-Chromium suite
-# passing with zero "Refused to execute" violations across every flow,
-# including the math-rendering test) — so hashing is safe here specifically.
-# It does NOT require touching any HTML/JS — the hashes are of the existing
-# inline content, computed by tools/csp/compute-csp-hashes.js.
-#
-# MAINTENANCE — READ BEFORE EDITING AN INLINE <script> BLOCK:
-# If you ever edit the text inside one of the 2 inline <script> blocks
-# (even whitespace), its hash changes and this CSP will silently block the
-# edited version in modern browsers. Run
-# `node tools/csp/compute-csp-hashes.js` to get the new hash, update the
-# Content-Security-Policy line below, and run `npm run verify:csp` (or let
-# CI do it) to confirm they're back in sync. verify:csp also fails on a
-# STALE hash (one that no longer matches any inline script), so the
-# allowlist can never be wider than what the pages really contain.
-#
-# If you fork this project and add an external CDN, web font, or analytics
-# script, you MUST widen connect-src/font-src/script-src accordingly, or
-# the browser will silently block it (which would look like an app bug but
-# would actually be this header).
-#
-# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-# HSTS SCOPE NOTE:
-# Strict-Transport-Security only has any effect when served over HTTPS —
-# browsers ignore it entirely on a plain HTTP response, so it is inert (not
-# harmful) on a local `http://` dev server and only takes effect once this
-# is actually deployed behind HTTPS. `includeSubDomains` is NOT set here
-# because that requires every subdomain of the deploying domain to also be
-# HTTPS-only, which is a fact about the *deployment* domain this repo has
-# no way to know — turn it on at the hosting layer once that is confirmed.
-# `preload` is deliberately omitted: submitting to the HSTS preload list is
-# a one-way, hard-to-reverse decision about a specific production domain,
-# not something a repository should opt a domain into on someone's behalf.
-
+# Same-origin scripts with exact hashes; MathJax CHTML needs dynamic inline styles.
+# No blanket inline-script permission. Public pages and mutable assets revalidate.
