-bar-chart values within their SVG. Four shell palette values were adjusted
-to improve practice text contrast. The shell includes:
-
-- `assets/js/theme.js` — a standalone theme module shared with the landing
-  page (same storage key `dynanca-mfc-theme-mode`). It no longer depends on
-  the engine having loaded.
-- A “← Practice catalog” link that returns to the last catalog view.
-- Real failure states (`practice/data-loader.js`): no `?quiz=`, unknown id,
-  bank not in this release, network failure, damaged or empty bank. Each
-  replaces “Loading…” with a status title, a link back to the catalog, and
-  “Try again” where retrying can help.
-
-Progress is stored per bank in this browser (`localStorage`); there is no
-account and no sync between devices.
-
-## Security headers (`_headers`)
-
-`script-src` allowlists the two inline scripts of `practice/index.html` by
-SHA-256; the landing page and `404.html` have no inline script or style.
-`style-src` deliberately keeps `'unsafe-inline'` **without any hash**:
-MathJax's CHTML output injects its stylesheet at runtime, and adding a hash
-would make browsers ignore `'unsafe-inline'` and break equation rendering.
-If you edit an inline script, run `node tools/csp/compute-csp-hashes.js`,
-update `_headers`, then `npm run verify:csp`.
-
-## Preview and deploy
-
-```
-npm run preview          # http://127.0.0.1:8788/  (sends _headers; CSP enforced)
-```
-
-Opening the files through `file://`, or with a server that ignores
-`_headers`, does not exercise the CSP.
-
-Cloudflare Pages settings (static site; no Functions, no Workers, no SPA
-fallback, no environment variables or secrets):
-
-| Setting | Value |
-|---|---|
-| Build command | `npm run build` |
-| Build output directory | `/` (the repository root) |
-
-`npm run build` regenerates `assets/data/bank-index.json` from the files
-being deployed, so a forgotten `npm run build:index` can no longer ship a
-stale index (CI still fails on a stale *committed* index via
-`verify:index` and `git diff --exit-code`). For a direct upload instead of a
-Git-connected project: `npm run build` locally, then
-`npx wrangler pages deploy . --project-name <your-project>`.
-
-Deploy the folder as static files, as before. Things that only a real
-Cloudflare deployment can confirm (check them on a preview deployment):
-
-- the headers in `_headers` are actually sent on every response;
-- Cloudflare redirects `…/practice/index.html?quiz=X` to
-  `…/practice/?quiz=X` — both forms are supported by the page;
-- `404.html` at the top level makes unknown paths return a real 404.
-  Without it Cloudflare Pages treats the site as a single-page app and
-  answers unknown URLs with the home page and HTTP 200. `404.html` uses
-  root-absolute asset paths, so it assumes the site is served from the
-  domain root.
-
-`node_modules/`, `test-results/`, `qa-evidence/` and `audit/` contain tools
-or review evidence and should be excluded from a production upload.
-The final ZIP contains them only where appropriate as source/evidence;
-installed dependencies and temporary test output are excluded.
-
-## Local rendering engine
-
-The practice UI needs no third-party runtime service:
-- local MathJax v3.2.1 (TeX → CHTML);
-- a local dependency-free SVG Venn renderer;
-- a local dependency-free SVG renderer for graphs, charts, coordinate
-  planes, number lines and basic geometry.
-
-### Bare-LaTeX auto-wrapping
-
-Some question text contains raw LaTeX commands (`\times`, `\frac`, …)
-without `\( \)`, `\[ \]` or `$$ $$` delimiters. This is handled once, at
-the rendering layer: `practice/practice-engine.js` exports
-`autoWrapBareLatex()`, called before any HTML is built. Content that
-already uses delimiters, or sits in code blocks, is left untouched. The
-validator's bare-LaTeX warning is a heads-up that this path is doing real
-work on real data — not something to "fix" by editing bank files.
-
-## Notes
-
-- **Completion and review are deterministic end states.** Answering the
-  last question shows “Quiz complete”; “Review mistakes” visits each missed
-  question once and ends. Covered by `tools/tests/run-tests.js` section 13
-  and `tests/browser/practice.spec.js`.
-- **Progress stats are scoped to the open bank.** Only question ids that
-  exist in the loaded bank are counted.
-- `tools/lib/csv-parse.js` and `tools/manifest-generator/` are legacy
-  (CSV era) and are only exercised by fixture tests.
-- `tools/practice-converter/convert-practices.js` is a one-off converter
-  for the pre-JSON question format; unrelated to the catalog.
